      }
    },
    {
      "id": 90,
      "text": "Must have histologically or cytologically confirmed progressive advanced/metastatic HER2-positive breast carcinoma as per the updated American Society of Clinical Oncology (ASCO) - College of American Pathologists (CAP) guidelines according to local testing. HER2 status may be determined in the primary breast cancer tumour or, when not available, in a metastatic lesion.",
      "logic": {
        "operator": "AND",
        "conditions": [
          {
            "field": "diagnosis",
            "operator": "=",
            "value": "breast carcinoma"
          },
          {
            "field": "molecular_status",
            "operator": "=",
            "value": "HER2-positive"
          },
          {
            "field": "stage",
            "operator": "=",
            "value": "advanced/metastatic"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 91,
      "text": "Multifocal unilateral or bilateral breast adenocarcinoma tumours are allowed if all tested HER2-positive, according to local testing",
      "logic": {
        "operator": "AND",
        "conditions": [
          {
            "field": "diagnosis",
            "operator": "=",
            "value": "breast adenocarcinoma"
          },
          {
            "field": "molecular_status",
            "operator": "=",
            "value": "HER2-positive"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 92,
      "text": "Prior treatment with taxane, trastuzumab and pertuzumab (early or advanced setting) and T-DXd (metastatic setting). In order to be eligible, patients subjects must have received T-DXd as the last systemic metastatic treatment line before inclusion, and presented disease progression on this drug.",
